list, who had lost in the final of the 1979 Worlds to Soviet " [:a {:href "/athletes/60504"} "Illia Mate"] ". Mate, however, would have been favored at any rate, also having won the 1979 European title. Another contender was Bulgarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/57472"} "Slavcho Chervenkov"] ", runner-up at the Europeans in 1979-80. Mate and Chervenkov both made the final round, joined there by Czechoslovak " [:a {:href "/athletes/60232"} "Július Strnisko"] ". Mate had won a close decision over Chervenkov in round four, 6-4, so when he defeated Strnisko by superior decision in the final, 15-3, Mate won the gold medal. Chervenkov also easily defeated Strnisko, 11-3, to take silver. Mate would win the 1982 World Championships, again defeating Chervenkov in the final round. Strnisko won two more bronze medals at the 1982-83 European Championships."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "253"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60504"} "Ilya Mate"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "35"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/57472"} "Slavcho Chervenkov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BUL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BUL.png"}] "BUL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "237"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60232"} "Július Strnisko"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/